This task class showed multiple demos with many colors and disconnected objects but only a small, consistent subset recolored. The useful transferable method is to inventory 4-connected components by color, recording size, bounding box, normalized shape, and changed/unchanged status. Compare transformed components across demonstrations, and use unchanged lookalikes as negative evidence. Test candidate triggers (shape identity, component size, relation/alignment to another object) against every demo's exact input/output delta before applying to the test.

Do not infer the destination-color mapping from proximity alone or from one visually salient example. Verify whether the transformation applies to a complete connected component or only matching cells/subcomponents. When two explanations remain viable, request a discriminating demo rather than submitting a speculative no-op or arbitrary recoloring. The session's hypotheses did not resolve the rule, so this note records only the validated analysis discipline—not a guessed transformation.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792484802/attempts/57865763327545bc884e27f058eb3817/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-solving/references/sparse-recoloring-component-analysis.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-solving", "file": "references/demo-budget-and-turn-discipline.md", "content": "# Demo-budget and turn discipline

In interactive ARC streams with one action per turn, every tool/action must earn its turn. A demo request is useful only when it separates explicit, competing hypotheses; after a demo arrives, parse its actual pair before requesting another. Do not emit empty scratch/tool calls or request demonstrations reflexively without stating internally what prediction they will distinguish. Keep the output contract in view: exactly one valid action JSON object on the final line.

The session that motivated this note used repeated demos but did not compare the returned pairs concretely before requesting further examples, and included non-informative tool calls. This is a process correction, not a task-specific transformation rule. Use the demo only to update hypotheses; once enough evidence exists, compute and validate the proposed output.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792484802/attempts/57865763327545bc884e27f058eb3817/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-solving/references/demo-budget-and-turn-discipline.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-solving", "file": "references/demo-delta-discipline.md", "content": "# Demo-delta discipline

In a motif/recoloring ARC task, reason from exact input-output changes before inferring the rule. Record changed coordinates and old/new colors, along with unchanged components. Test candidate operations against every changed and unchanged cell; a visual resemblance between an embedded shape and another cluster is not enough evidence for stamping, copying, or recoloring.

After an incorrect submission, treat the feedback as rejection of the candidate rule. Avoid a minor variation of the same unsupported hypothesis. Request another demo when the remaining examples could distinguish plausible rules, and budget demos against the cost of another wrong submission. The final task attempt here was still unresolved, so this note captures only the validated procedural lesson, not a guessed transformation.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792484802/attempts/57865763327545bc884e27f058eb3817/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-solving/references/demo-delta-discipline.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-solving", "file": "references/recurrent-instance-overgeneralization.md", "content": "# Recurrent instances: avoid transferring unverified rules

Task IDs may recur while each instance supplies a fresh test grid and demonstrations. Treat prior-session/task-ID notes as candidate hypotheses only. Re-derive the motif and operation from current-instance input/output deltas before applying any remembered rule.

After a wrong submission, explicitly reject the full hypothesis. Do not keep changing one parameter at a time (stencil crop, anchor, or background match color) without new evidence. Compare exact changed and unchanged cells across all available demos; validate one complete rule against each pair before submitting. If the demos do not determine a rule, spend a demo request only when it can distinguish concrete competing hypotheses; once the cap is reached, avoid brute-force submissions.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792484802/attempts/57865763327545bc884e27f058eb3817/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-solving/references/recurrent-instance-overgeneralization.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-solving", "file": "references/lesson-demo-request-discipline.md", "content": "# Demo requests should be hypothesis-driven

A demonstration request spends budget and should resolve a concrete uncertainty. Before requesting one, state internally at least two plausible hypotheses and what different input/output evidence each predicts. After the pair arrives, compare it cell by cell with those predictions and update or reject hypotheses before choosing the next action. Do not fall into a reflexive cycle of requesting another pair without incorporating the latest evidence. Once the cap is exhausted, stop requesting and submit only a rule that has been tested against every available example; after an incorrect submission, reject the tested rule rather than making small unsupported variations.

In one difficult instance, repeated requests were made without extracting a valid rule, and several speculative submissions followed. The transferable learning is the decision discipline above, not the guesses made in that instance.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792484802/attempts/57865763327545bc884e27f058eb3817/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-solving/references/lesson-demo-request-discipline.md"}

